       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for a dose that is twice the maximum daily limit. At 6,400 mg/day the patient would face a serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. I can't see a benefit that would justify that risk, and a higher dose won't give more pain or anti-inflammatory relief.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth four times daily.** This is 3,200 mg/day, the maximum. I can add a note to take it with food.\n- **Enter a lower standard dose**, such as 400\u2013800 mg three times daily.\n- **Help with a different goal.** If the patient's pain or inflammation is poorly controlled, I can enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at a safe dose.\n- **Get a second review.** If you think this dose is needed, a pharmacist or attending can review it. If they approve it, it would need to go through their documented override process.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it now."
